173
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,250
So quiz, Marco.

174
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:03,010
What is the first thing that a paramedic does when he or she finds a body in an emergency?

175
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:07,200
What paramedic checks for a pulse to make sure you're alive, right?

176
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,200
Right.

177
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,200
A pulse.

178
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,000
So, dum, dum, dum, dum.

179
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,330
The pulse is the rhythm, that's the sound of your heart pumping blood.

180
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:20,320
And you can feel someone's wrist or their throat.

181
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:24,900
So to check for a pulse means to check and make sure their heart is pumping blood.

182
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:25,420
Right.

183
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:34,880
And not only that, but to make sure that the heart is pumping blood relatively normal because sometimes your heart can be pumping blood too fast or too slow.

184
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:38,040
And if it's too slow, it's very possible that you will faint.

185
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:39,400
Very good.

186
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,200
All right.

187
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,200
So we check for a pulse.

188
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:42,980
Now, what else happens?

189
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:52,280
Well, if there's a very serious emergency and the paramedic needs help to give aid to the person who is injured, then they will rush that person to the hospital.

190
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:52,920
Okay.

191
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,800
So the verb to rush, what does that mean?

192
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:03,620
All right, so to rush someone or to rush someone to the hospital means to take someone or to go with someone very, very quickly.

193
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:04,740
Okay.

194
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,860
So let's give an example.

195
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:11,880
I could say, listen, Marco, I don't want to rush you, but I really need the report done today.

196
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,600
Or I could say, I need to rush home.

197
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,320
My parents need me.

198
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:20,240
Or if a woman is having a baby, you want to rush her to the emergency room.

199
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:21,640
Right.

200
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,640
Okay.

201
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,640
So you need to go quickly.

202
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:23,880
All right.

203
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:31,960
So when we're talking about fainting, the person said, before he used the word faint, he said, I tend to faint.

204
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:32,770
Okay.

205
00:09:32,890 --> 00:09:33,870
I tend to.

206
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:40,170
I tend to is a really great verb that describes a normal or habitual behavior.

207
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:45,910
That's like saying, I tend to faint when it's very, very hot outside.

208
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:49,790
That means I often faint when it's very, very hot outside.

209
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,490
It's something that happens normally.

210
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,410
So it's a tendency.

211
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,840
Right.

212
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,130
It's not for everyone.

213
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:54,970
It's for me.

214
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,310
So I tend to.

215
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,350
